---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="What is Kitfy"
  description="Kitfy is ten small web tools kept in one place, built by one developer, funded by ads instead of subscriptions."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-(--container-content) px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-[68ch]">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-display font-bold tracking-(--tracking-display) text-fg">What is Kitfy</h1>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-6 font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-secondary">
        <p>
          Kitfy is ten small web tools kept in one place. Each one solves a single problem that comes up during a
          normal working day, like a video that is too big to send or a bank statement that arrived as a PDF when
          you needed a spreadsheet.
        </p>
        <p>
          They are separate sites with their own domains. Kitfy is the shelf they sit on, so you only have to
          remember one address instead of ten.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-display font-bold tracking-(--tracking-display) text-fg">
          Why they run in the browser
        </h2>
        <p>
          Most tools like these upload your file to a server, do the work there, and send it back. That is slower,
          and it means a document you did not want to share has been sitting on someone else's machine. Kitfy's
          tools use the browser's own capabilities instead, so the file is never transmitted. It is faster on large
          files and there is nothing to trust.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-display font-bold tracking-(--tracking-display) text-fg">How it is paid for</h2>
        <p>
          Ads on the pages, not subscriptions. Nothing is behind a signup and no feature is held back for a paid
          tier, because there is no paid tier.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-display font-bold tracking-(--tracking-display) text-fg">Who builds it</h2>
        <p>
          One developer, working on these in the open. If a tool is broken or you want one that does not exist yet,
          the <a href="mailto:hello@kitfy.work" class="text-fg underline underline-offset-4">contact link</a> in the
          footer reaches a real inbox.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
